Inlaw Biker wrote:

> aris73 wrote:
> 
>>Why isn't + sufficient for spell ordering?
> 
> 
> It's sort of a pain, but I don't think it begs for fixing.  "+" is
> enough to order the spells however you like.  Personally I like them
> sorted by type, from lowest to highest level, and will the spells I
> never use on page 2.

And because it doesn't let you assign a letter other than in the 
sequence of how many spells you've learned.

Let's say that I like to have magic missile on 'a', force bolt on 'b' 
and detect monsters on 'd'. I start a new wizard character and it 
happens to have spellbook of detect monster. I can adjust force bolt on 
'b' but then my detect monster is on 'a'. I cannot adjust detect monster 
on 'd' before I've learned two other spells.

What I would like is that one can adjust the learned spells to whatever 
in the range 'a-zA-Z0-9' (and maybe all the rest of the printing 
characters). When you learn a new spell the game asks what letter you 
want to assign it, with the lowest availabe as a default.

I might even try to make such patch when I have suitable time available.

